{"id": "EUVD-2026-37784", "enisaUuid": "c609e819-55a4-3005-9c1e-67a935f31527", "description": "libssh2 1.11.1, fixed in commit 97acf3d, contains an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in ssh2_transport_read() that fails to enforce upper bounds on packet_length field. Remote attackers can send crafted SSH packets with excessively large packet_length values to corrupt heap memory and achieve remote code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-06-17T19:03:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T18:33:35", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/pull/2052", "https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2/commit/97acf3dfda80c91c3a8c9f2372546301d4a1a7a8", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libssh2-out-of-bounds-write-via-unchecked-packet-length-in-transport-c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r8mh-x5qv-7gg2", "CVE-2026-55200"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 4.02, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3068bf62-9921-36c7-9cb3-25b8a4d0fb44", "product": {"name": "libssh2", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "1.11.1"}, {"id": "b339019c-ec59-3520-a72b-f8aa146803b6", "product": {"name": "libssh2", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "1c3f1b7da588f2652260285529ec3c1f1125eb4e <97acf3dfda80c91c3a8c9f2372546301d4a1a7a8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "84c8cadb-2bd8-365b-aab4-16fc8df3133a", "vendor": {"name": "libssh2"}}], "isExploited": false}